DSE — Digital Specialist Engineer
SP L1 — Specialist Programmer Level 1
SP L2 — Specialist Programmer Level 2
SP L3 — Specialist Programmer Level 3

 Internal target                 Expected interview standard                                                                                       
 DSE-ready       | Strong fundamentals, clean easy/medium coding, SQL, OOP, project explanation                                      
 SP L1-ready     | Consistent medium DSA, optimisation, strong CS fundamentals                                                       
 SP L2-ready     | Medium-hard DSA, DP, graphs, trees, deeper project and design reasoning                                           
 SP L3-ready     | Hard/complex problem-solving, multiple approaches, proof of correctness, excellent optimisation and communication 

For the next 30 days:

Minimum six focused hours every day:: No copied code and no watching solutions before completing a genuine attempt.

Every solution must include:
Brute-force approach
Optimised approach
Time complexity
Space complexity
Edge cases
Dry run
Students must code in one primary language only during the interview preparation
Every student must explain their project without reading from the résumé
Attendance without performance receives no credit
Every incorrect question goes into an error notebook
Every Sunday is an elimination-style mock interview
Students who repeatedly fail basics return to foundation training immediately
No student says, “I know the concept,” unless they can explain it and code it


